HSET trail:062 name "Quartz Headland Path" region "Pacific Coast" difficulty "easy" features "coast,forest,waterfall,views,wildlife,kid_friendly" distance_km 1.7 elevation_gain_m 100 description "Quartz Headland Path traces the edge of high sea cliffs, with waves crashing below and harbor seals often visible offshore. The first stretch passes through cool forest of Sitka spruce. A short side path leads to a small waterfall that is worth the detour. The path is wide and nearly level, covering 1.7 km with only 100 m of climbing. Several viewpoints open up wide vistas over the surrounding valleys. Watch for harbor seals, especially early in the morning. Kids love the short distance and the little bridges, so bring a picnic and take your time. Snow lingers on the upper section until early summer, so check conditions before you go." description_embedding "W\xbci\xbd\xf3\x27\xf7\xbb\xcb!\xf3\xbdH\x8c)\xbe]\xf3\x87<\xfbYo>\xa9\x16\x8b\xbc\x02\xee9=i\xd1\xe5\xbd\xbd\xdfM\xbe\x0e\xf5:\xbe\x20\x9a\x1c\xbe\xc1\xf6\x8d\xbe\xcbj\x95=\x03GH\xbd\xadq\xcb=\xdb\xd1:>b\x8a\xed=\xb4\xe9\x27\xbdH\xe5v\xbd\xddq\xa9\xbd\x07\x94+>/&\x1b>\xc4\x99\x01>\xa7\x05\x80<`RT\xbd\xbc\xb59=\x9a\x09\xed==\xcb\xe8;S\x85\x9a;\xab{\x7f<g\xb7\xb3;\xa9y\xd2=$+N\xbd2\xa9\xed\xbd\xc9\xe8\x08\xbe\x14#H\xbd\x13D\xf9=u/\xb0=S\x92t>\xf5P\x1b>\xf3l\xe2\xbc\xd8\xc0\xfd;\xb3fO>\x8e\x86\xf4\xbdgb\xc1=H\xdc\xaf=\x11H\xa9\xbc\x8d\x9eV>\x0d\xf2+\xbcB\xea\xe1\xbd\x5c\xd00>p#T<mSS>f\xef\xe5\xbd>\xf3\x8f\xbc\xd8\xd4\xce=cP\xb7=\xd1\xd4\xe9\xbd\x84\xf5M\xbe\xc8\xd2c=\xd8\xccD>\x18\xbc\x22\xbe\x96ja>"
HSET trail:063 name "Willow Lakes Basin" region "Great Lakes" difficulty "easy" features "lake,waterfall,wildflowers,wildlife,dog_friendly,camping,quiet" distance_km 3.2 elevation_gain_m 80 description "Willow Lakes Basin climbs gently to a clear lake ringed by sugar maple, with a pebbly shore made for a long lunch. A short side path leads to a small waterfall that is worth the detour. The path is wide and nearly level, covering 3.2 km with only 80 m of climbing. In early summer the slopes are bright with blueberry blossoms. Watch for bald eagles, especially early in the morning. Dogs are welcome on a leash, and there is fresh water for them along the way. A few tent sites near the water allow a relaxed overnight under a starry sky. Few people make it this far, so solitude is almost guaranteed on weekdays." description_embedding "I*\x19>\xf0\x1c>=\x10\xfd\xf9\xbd\xa1\xcf\x02\xbeb>s\xbd\xc3\xd2\xbd\xbd\xd6\xfd\x0a\xbe\xf2\xaa,\xbe/\x02\x0b\xbe\x88hh\xbew\x82\x1d\xbe\xaeRP\xbd\x9bo\xa2\xbe\xfd\x8d9\xbc\xe2gn\xbd\xdd\xe3\x81=\x9b\x10R>\x13\x1a\x91\xbd\xa4\xde1<kk\xa1<\x22\xa5\x8d<\xcc\x8b\xff\xbd?\x93\x89>\x9e\xb5\x8a=>Hi>\x1b$\xf3<w\x9d&\xbeTl\xe0<\x86\xd1\xab\xbdaa\x82\xbd\xae\xfd\x16\xbecDW>\xfaY*=\xa9f\xdb\xba\xb0\x80\x0c<\x86>m\xbd\x8b\x91\xe6\xbd\x8dT\x03>J\x84!=\x9dCS>|%\x83=C\xb1\xfa=\xf2!\xac=\xa5N\x0a>\x96\xe2\x00\xbc\x9b\xd5\xf1=\xffJE>\x90n\xd1=\xc2\xa4\x94=\xc55\xbe=\xee\x0a\x16\xbe\x8c\xab*>\x86\x82\xde\xbd\xb5\x1d\x0e\xbc1\xd8;>-\x13\xe8\xbd\xd1\xc3\x8f\xbd\x98&t\xbd>\xd7\xff\xbd\xf5#\x11\xbd\x82\xf2\xfc;.\xd3#\xbc&Ve\xbec\x829="
